; Network-effect boundary for one explicitly selected Go declaration.
;
; This is the shipped specialization. Its ship-time declaration selection is
; the empty set, so a repository that enables this policy without editing the
; selection block below carries no purity obligation at all. Purity is never
; inferred from a function name, a file name, a comment, or an unqualified
; annotation.
;
; Activation
; ----------
; 1. The reviewed Go model is already shipped: the embedded
;    `bifrost.go.stdlib.net-http` pack declares `bifrost.network_io` on
;    `net/http.Get` at its written arity one, and the sibling
;    `bifrost.go.stdlib.net-http-declarations` pack publishes that exact
;    package function so the Go resolver can bind it. Unlike the JavaScript,
;    TypeScript and Python rows there is no separate file to install under
;    `.bifrost/semantic-models/`: Go publishes one `net/http` declaration
;    surface, and a second activated pack declaring the same package would make
;    the overlay lookup ambiguous and fail closed for every `net/http` call.
; 2. Replace both declaration selections in the analysis block below with the
;    exact declaration(s) this repository protects, for example:
;      (language go (enclosing-decl (function :name "Total")))
; 3. Enable the policy: `bifrost --policy-id
;    bifrost.effects.go.selected-boundary-no-network-io --fail-on error`.
;
; API choice: `net/http.Get` at its written arity one. It is the
; package-function route, which the Go import binder proves by expanding the
; call site's `http` qualifier to the `net/http` import path before the
; declaration overlay is consulted, so the identity never rests on the
; spelling `Get`. `(*http.Client).Do` would bind through the concrete-receiver
; route instead, but it needs a receiver whose `*http.Client` type the analyzer
; must first agree on, so the package function is the simpler exact identity.
;
; The rule body is shared across languages; only the language label, the
; activated model, and this selection block differ.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.effects.go.selected-boundary-no-network-io"
  :name "Selected Go boundary reaches no network effect"
  :message "the selected Go boundary reaches the declared network effect"
  :severity error
  :description "One explicitly selected Go declaration must not reach a declared network effect, directly or through workspace helpers. The effect is declared by a reviewed semantic model on the exact external API identity, never inferred from a function name, a file name, a comment, or an unqualified annotation. The ship-time selection is empty; configure the declaration-selection block before enabling this policy."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#network-effect-boundary"
  :tags ["effects" "network" "boundary" "go"]
  :analysis
    (analysis
      :type assertion
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      ; Declaration-selection block. Ship-time selection: the empty set.
      ; Replace both `(except ...)` expressions below with the exact
      ; declaration this repository protects. The `effect` binding repeats the
      ; same selection on purpose: `procedure-effects` derives a closure for
      ; every declaration its input query returns, so repeating the selection
      ; is what keeps the policy from deriving effects for declarations it did
      ; not select. With the ship-time empty selection it derives none, the
      ; assertion has no group to judge, and the run is vacuously clean.
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      (bind :name selected
        :query (rql :schema-version 1
          (language go
            (except
              (enclosing-decl (function))
              (enclosing-decl (function))))))
      (bind :name effect
        :query (rql :schema-version 1
          (language go
            (procedure-effects
              (except
                (enclosing-decl (function))
                (enclosing-decl (function)))))))
      (join :left selected :right effect :on ((id procedure_id)))
      (group :name selected-boundary :by (selected.id)
        (aggregate :name network-effects :op count
          :where ((effect.effect_id eq "bifrost.network_io")
                  (effect.derivation eq declared))))
      (assert :group selected-boundary :value network-effects :cardinality (exactly 0))))
